Congratulations. Total money, $0.

00:50:14.820 --> 00:50:16.960
And I think, yeah, I think that's cool.

00:50:16.960 --> 00:50:31.960
It's obviously an Easter egg slash, like, dog ending, but I was actually watching, like, you know, just to see what the – not to see the consensus because I know that everybody kind of loves this game.

00:50:32.120 --> 00:50:41.560
But just to see what other people have to say about it, I was watching a video of a guy that was really annoyed by the fact that this was so out of the way and almost impossible.

00:50:41.560 --> 00:50:49.200
Like, well, if you're a completionist, you won't be able to see this unless you do this really boring and long, tedious process.

00:50:49.400 --> 00:50:50.940
I'm like, dude, it's an Easter egg.

00:50:51.200 --> 00:50:54.340
And the fact that it's there is more just like, oh, cool.

00:50:54.440 --> 00:51:03.680
They actually thought of, yeah, the implications of this and not so much, like, hit it as an achievement for the people that are OCD about achievements.

00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:05.640
So I thought it was cool.

00:51:06.700 --> 00:51:13.560
Yeah, it almost feels like something nobody would have known about for a long time if they didn't reveal it themselves somewhere.

00:51:13.820 --> 00:51:21.320
You know, like, how would you even – the objective of the game is to collect some form of money, and money is given out so much in this game.

00:51:21.520 --> 00:51:23.180
You know, like, millions of dollars.

00:51:23.340 --> 00:51:25.120
How are you going to get to zero?

00:51:25.120 --> 00:51:34.660
So it actually provides, like, I don't know, a unique replayability for someone who might find out about this having not played it in the last, like, you know, 20 years.

00:51:34.940 --> 00:51:38.060
Being like, oh, I want to go back, and now I have, like, an added challenge.

00:51:38.180 --> 00:51:43.060
It almost feels like the Kirby games, which are super easy no matter which console they've ever been on.

00:51:43.120 --> 00:51:44.960
They've never made a hard Kirby game.

00:51:44.980 --> 00:51:49.700
But once you beat the game, all fans of Kirby know that's when the game starts.

00:51:49.700 --> 00:51:55.300
Now there's, like, a new challenge mode where, like, you can find out the ending where Kirby fights God.

00:51:55.620 --> 00:51:56.580
It always happens.

00:51:56.760 --> 00:51:57.880
I'm not joking. Is this really?

00:51:58.080 --> 00:51:58.980
Okay, I did not know that.

00:51:59.300 --> 00:52:05.540
Yeah, Kirby always fights, like, some kind of, like, you know, eldritch horror style thing.

00:52:05.740 --> 00:52:07.080
Like, yeah, just crazy.

00:52:07.180 --> 00:52:11.220
But it's a final boss that's, like, secretly locked behind, like, 100% completion.

00:52:11.480 --> 00:52:15.180
Wow. Anyway, a little more on the ending here.

00:52:15.180 --> 00:52:16.040
It's not over yet.

00:52:16.040 --> 00:52:29.760
Besides all those alternate endings, I think it was, this was one year ago, Destructoid did an article where they were talking with Darlene Lacey, who was in charge of overseeing all the Disney games that were being made.

00:52:29.880 --> 00:52:34.800
Not just on the NES, but any kind of Disney video game properties in the late 80s.

00:52:34.800 --> 00:52:52.300
And Darlene recalls that they had to make a change to the game's ending because Disney did not like it, where originally there was going to be an option for Scrooge to give up his fortune and inform his nephews there really is more important treasure than this.

00:52:52.300 --> 00:52:54.780
And that is dreams and friends.

00:52:56.280 --> 00:53:08.440
And, you know, they were tempted to keep it in, but that is just so, you know, so against everything Scrooge McDuck or Uncle Scrooge, Uncle McDuck or whatever you call him.

00:53:09.620 --> 00:53:12.320
Uncle Scrooge is like a real person in the Christmas Carol.

00:53:12.320 --> 00:53:13.760
I don't feel right calling him that.

00:53:14.280 --> 00:53:15.340
But, yeah, it is.

00:53:15.480 --> 00:53:16.700
It's just out of character.

00:53:16.700 --> 00:53:18.780
And say whatever you want.

00:53:18.900 --> 00:53:24.560
And like, oh, that's, of course, Disney, the conglomerate, would say this is a bad thing.

00:53:24.640 --> 00:53:26.480
But like, no, it's just Scrooge McDuck.

00:53:26.580 --> 00:53:27.540
He would never do that.

00:53:28.220 --> 00:53:30.280
That's his one personality trait.

00:53:30.560 --> 00:53:33.040
But he still does say something somewhat nice.

00:53:33.060 --> 00:53:35.620
He says, I couldn't have done it without you.

00:53:35.620 --> 00:53:37.660
I really am the richest duck in the world.

00:53:38.060 --> 00:53:40.880
He should have maybe said we are the richest ducks in the world.

00:53:40.880 --> 00:53:51.020
No, no, no. I think that's like, you know, I have profited off of your labor, but you're not going to get any.

00:53:51.380 --> 00:53:53.420
Oh, it's some like late stage capitalism.

00:53:53.940 --> 00:53:55.180
Well, I got that.

00:53:55.240 --> 00:54:00.500
I mean, I think what they were, yeah, they're obviously trying to do the like, I am the richest duck in the world because I have you guys.

00:54:00.720 --> 00:54:08.040
But what I gather from that, because I'm just watching this ending now on YouTube, and, you know, they say like, hooray, Uncle Scrooge, we're glad you found it.

00:54:08.120 --> 00:54:09.560
Like, but don't forget, we helped too.

00:54:09.560 --> 00:54:11.640
Like, almost like they're expecting like a cut.

00:54:11.780 --> 00:54:13.060
And then he's just like, you're right.

00:54:13.180 --> 00:54:14.600
Thanks. You guys are great.

00:54:15.300 --> 00:54:16.740
And then it doesn't give him anything.

00:54:17.300 --> 00:54:19.960
Yeah. And then it brags about how rich he is.

00:54:20.400 --> 00:54:23.840
Honestly, how is this guy a hero?

00:54:23.840 --> 00:54:29.640
I don't know. This was just that time before, you know, the, before social media.

00:54:32.380 --> 00:54:33.840
It's really a character study.

00:54:33.840 --> 00:54:35.140
I idolized Scrooge McDuck.

00:54:40.460 --> 00:54:48.660
On the sequels and spinoff side, if you ever want to check out DuckTales in portable form, there is the Game Boy version of DuckTales.

00:54:48.800 --> 00:54:50.020
And it is a straight port.

00:54:50.220 --> 00:54:58.140
They changed a little bit, I guess, like how the levels, like how the size of them, because you scroll, like everything's bigger on the Game Boy.

00:54:58.260 --> 00:54:59.640
So you just see less information.

00:54:59.640 --> 00:55:02.880
So other than that, like it is basically the same exact game.

00:55:03.060 --> 00:55:06.160
So it's pretty cool that it's a very faithful port on the go.

00:55:06.160 --> 00:55:10.920
If you're a big fan of the console version and now you're going to your aunt's, it's like, hey, you got something for the car ride.

00:55:11.780 --> 00:55:13.660
But that's not the only thing for DuckTales.

00:55:13.860 --> 00:55:19.900
We will play, I think, as Joe, I think you knew this, but you did mention that maybe it's something they could fix in the sequel.

00:55:19.900 --> 00:55:27.320
We'll find out if they fix anything in DuckTales 2, which is on the NES, and a very expensive game, I might add.

00:55:27.620 --> 00:55:29.040
Uh-oh. Hmm.

00:55:29.400 --> 00:55:35.520
Yeah, I don't know how we're going to afford it, but we'll give it our best go to, because, you know, we all legally buy these games before we play them.

00:55:35.640 --> 00:55:37.960
I don't know why you would, but it goes without saying.

00:55:38.120 --> 00:55:40.880
Is there other ways to get these games?

00:55:41.260 --> 00:55:42.320
Not that I know of.

00:55:42.320 --> 00:55:54.100
And if you wanted to legally buy other DuckTales games, you could do that on PSN, Xbox Live Arcade, on your Wii U, which I believe they just shut that whole system down, so you can't do it there anymore.

00:55:54.160 --> 00:56:00.940
But it's still available on Steam, because in summer of 2013, DuckTales Remastered came out.

00:56:00.940 --> 00:56:12.860
And the remake includes modified versions of the original levels, plus some additional levels, completely animated cutscenes with voice acting of the surviving original cast.

00:56:12.860 --> 00:56:18.440
And by that, I guess they just mean whoever is still alive, you know, they got to sign on to do the roles.

00:56:18.660 --> 00:56:22.440
Anybody who, you know, they didn't recast or anything like that, I imagine, unless they had to.

00:56:22.660 --> 00:56:26.440
But they're not saying that canon Scrooge McDuck is actually dead.

00:56:27.240 --> 00:56:28.360
Yes, yeah, exactly.

00:56:28.360 --> 00:56:46.920
But, you know, one thing I found interesting is they took the time in the cutscenes, now that they have voice acting and everything, to explain a lot of, like, the plot and stuff that necessarily didn't need any explaining for a series based around ducks.

00:56:46.920 --> 00:56:53.960
But they felt the need to explain how Scrooge McDuck is able to be on the moon without a helmet.

00:56:53.960 --> 00:57:07.780
And that is because the Gizmo Duck, or whatever his name is, the one who invents all the gadgets, he has invented a chewing gum that you just take five chews of, and then you can be on the moon for an hour.

00:57:07.780 --> 00:57:21.260
I would have thought that since it's implied that the moon is made out of cheese, that it was actually just like, you know, from the gases that emanate from cheese, an atmosphere has formed.

00:57:22.140 --> 00:57:24.680
But maybe that's too deep lore.

00:57:24.800 --> 00:57:40.240
I don't know. One other really cool thing about DuckTales Remastered is the look of the game, in my opinion, because they did do this 2.5D style level graphics for the backgrounds and the platforms.

00:57:40.240 --> 00:57:47.780
But the ducks and the enemies are all still in that, like, classic cartoon style look.

00:57:47.880 --> 00:57:56.840
They almost look like, not quite like Paper Mario-like characters, and definitely not like their 8-bit pixel art that we expect from the DuckTales on the NES.

00:57:57.060 --> 00:58:03.640
But it's like a nice bridge, so this way it's not super jarring to see, like, a 3D version of Scrooge McDuck.

00:58:03.880 --> 00:58:07.520
You know, it feels a little classic in that regard, so I appreciated that.

00:58:07.520 --> 00:58:13.340
The original 8-bit version of DuckTales can still be played today if you don't have an NES anymore.

00:58:13.340 --> 00:58:17.540
You can still play it because it was included on the Disney Afternoon Collection.

00:58:17.780 --> 00:58:23.200
And maybe they call it the Afternoon Collection because it takes just an entire afternoon to beat the game.

00:58:23.540 --> 00:58:27.380
But you can play that on PC, PlayStation 4, and Xbox One.

00:58:28.100 --> 00:58:31.440
So, you know, it's pretty accessible, this game, in 2022.

00:58:31.720 --> 00:58:40.160
Lots of options. And Mike, I think it's called the Disney Afternoon Collection because they're all based on Disney Afternoon cartoons.

00:58:40.460 --> 00:58:41.280
Like, that block.

00:58:41.540 --> 00:58:42.740
That TV block.

00:58:43.300 --> 00:58:49.060
You know, you, between this and Quackula, you're making just enough sense.

00:58:49.060 --> 00:58:54.480
But I still can't say, you know, that everybody else agrees because they didn't name him Quackula.

00:58:55.020 --> 00:58:55.840
That's true.

00:58:56.080 --> 00:58:59.300
If he were named Quackula, I would agree with you on the afternoon thing.

00:58:59.620 --> 00:59:00.740
Okay, yeah.

00:59:00.740 --> 00:59:03.700
We'll have to see if everybody agrees on just one more thing.

00:59:03.700 --> 00:59:07.100
And it's probably the most important thing we do on Nostalgia.

00:59:07.340 --> 00:59:13.040
We're going to see if everyone can agree on whether DuckTales belongs on the Essential Games list.

00:59:15.700 --> 00:59:19.400
Sean, your vote for DuckTales on the Essential Games list.

00:59:20.460 --> 00:59:25.800
Okay, but before I go into this fully, I just need to...

00:59:25.800 --> 00:59:31.820
Like, we did, like, allude to it in the beginning, but we didn't really spend much time on it.

00:59:31.920 --> 00:59:35.400
Like, the music in this game is incredible.

00:59:35.700 --> 00:59:36.720
Like, they're actual songs.

00:59:36.720 --> 00:59:41.000
It's not just the moon level that has a banger.

00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:48.060
It's kind of all of them, aside from a couple, like, you know, a couple things that just sound annoying.

00:59:48.280 --> 00:59:49.360
But those aren't level songs.

00:59:49.440 --> 00:59:50.980
Those are just, like, weird tracks.

00:59:51.180 --> 00:59:56.600
But just wanted to state that because it does also inform my opinion on the Essential Games list.

00:59:58.680 --> 01:00:02.380
There's some stuff that, you know, we said that there were kind of missed opportunities.

01:00:02.560 --> 01:00:12.420
But it's only, like, good games that can have these kinds of missed opportunities.

01:00:12.720 --> 01:00:17.300
A lot of the times we're talking about a game that is so bad that, like, you know,

01:00:17.440 --> 01:00:25.100
they had so many opportunities to make it good, whereas this is a great game that had opportunities to become amazing.

01:00:25.960 --> 01:00:29.400
I think, yes, it's a lot easier than one would expect.

01:00:29.820 --> 01:00:41.020
But I think that just the whole experience of this game between the way he controls, the level design, the goofy animations,

01:00:42.180 --> 01:00:46.040
that everything about it is just fun.

01:00:46.460 --> 01:00:50.400
And maybe it's not always challenging, but it is always fun.

01:00:50.400 --> 01:00:56.640
And for all these reasons and probably more, I'm going to put this on the Essential Games list.

01:00:56.860 --> 01:00:58.100
For my – I'm sorry.

01:00:58.160 --> 01:01:00.540
I'm going to vote for it to be on the Essential Games list.

01:01:01.320 --> 01:01:02.980
You're getting a little ahead of yourself.

01:01:02.980 --> 01:01:04.180
Yeah, that's me.

01:01:05.620 --> 01:01:07.160
Joe, your vote.

01:01:08.020 --> 01:01:13.060
So, like I said, I mean, I really, really appreciate a game that does something different.

01:01:13.180 --> 01:01:19.320
And this control scheme and the way the platforming feels is not only, like, good, but it's unique.

01:01:19.320 --> 01:01:21.100
It's different than other games that I've played.

01:01:21.520 --> 01:01:24.580
And, like, even the way you attack is different in a good way.

01:01:25.480 --> 01:01:28.980
And, like, the nonlinear levels are fun and interesting to explore.

01:01:28.980 --> 01:01:36.300
And, like, just the fact that it encouraged me to try and get a better score says something about it.

01:01:37.240 --> 01:01:41.580
And I'll say, like, absolutely – I struggled with this vote.

01:01:41.680 --> 01:01:43.120
So, I'm going to say this.

01:01:43.220 --> 01:01:47.620
Like, definitely no question that this is an Essential NES game.

01:01:48.760 --> 01:01:51.120
But is it an Essential game today?

01:01:51.120 --> 01:01:57.920
Does it hold up against modern games, even, like, games that maybe were inspired by DuckTales that might have improved it?

01:01:57.920 --> 01:02:01.180
But I was on the fence because, you know, I've got my golden plates.

01:02:01.240 --> 01:02:02.540
And I was like, I can put it there.

01:02:02.680 --> 01:02:10.340
And then I was also like – I could make my – you know, coin my new category, which is Essential game but on probation.

01:02:10.960 --> 01:02:17.740
And I sort of wanted to do that and think about, like, in the best of 89, maybe I'll take it off or maybe I'll revisit it.

01:02:19.120 --> 01:02:26.520
But I think when it comes down to it, I feel like a lot of these themes just could have been taken a little further.

01:02:26.520 --> 01:02:28.320
I just wanted a little more out of this game.

01:02:28.560 --> 01:02:32.340
And, like, it's kind of like what I said – and help me out here.

01:02:32.480 --> 01:02:33.540
What was the last game?

01:02:33.660 --> 01:02:36.080
Sean, you voted for it to be Essential and Mike and I didn't.

01:02:36.140 --> 01:02:37.080
What game was that?

01:02:37.480 --> 01:02:38.600
Yeah. A couple weeks ago.

01:02:39.640 --> 01:02:41.700
I have a very short memory, Joe.

01:02:41.840 --> 01:02:43.160
Me too. What the heck was it?

01:02:43.160 --> 01:02:44.700
I said the same thing about that.

01:02:44.800 --> 01:02:50.220
That, like, I don't have anything – I don't have anything particularly bad to say about DuckTales.

01:02:50.300 --> 01:02:51.180
I think it's fantastic. Fantastic.

01:02:51.540 --> 01:02:58.760
I just don't think it's quite on the level where I'm going to decide, like, this is up there with the other games on the Essential games list.

01:02:58.860 --> 01:03:00.140
That, like, you must play it.

01:03:00.300 --> 01:03:02.900
I think if you want to play an NES game, definitely play it.

01:03:02.980 --> 01:03:08.160
And if you can get your hands on it, it's a – we haven't really used this term in a while, but it's a play it for sure.

01:03:08.280 --> 01:03:09.540
A golden play it.

01:03:09.540 --> 01:03:15.200
But I don't know if I – I don't know if I get behind it being up there with all these other games we have on the Essential games list.

01:03:15.280 --> 01:03:22.900
And I know that that might rub some people the wrong way because while looking into this game, I realized that it has a very big fouling and people really, really love it.

01:03:24.280 --> 01:03:26.900
Like I said, I appreciate everything it's doing.

01:03:26.900 --> 01:03:29.700
I just don't think it – I don't think it quite reaches that level.

01:03:29.840 --> 01:03:32.300
And I'm hoping DuckTales 2 gets us there.

01:03:34.680 --> 01:03:37.980
Sean tried to put the black bass on the Essential games list.

01:03:37.980 --> 01:03:38.840
No, I didn't.

01:03:38.840 --> 01:03:39.980
That was the one. Of course.

01:03:40.800 --> 01:03:43.200
That was the one that Joe was like, no, of course not.

01:03:43.320 --> 01:03:44.760
It was Air Fortress.

01:03:44.860 --> 01:03:49.740
Air Fortress. I just thought that would be funny if people go back to the black bass.

01:03:49.900 --> 01:03:52.140
Because, you know, they probably jumped out of that episode.

01:03:52.140 --> 01:03:54.420
They were like, oh, yeah, yeah, we know this isn't essential.

01:03:54.560 --> 01:03:56.080
But now they're like, wait, Sean said what?

01:03:57.080 --> 01:03:58.060
It's actually good?

01:03:58.780 --> 01:04:03.880
Anyway, no, to round this out, you know, Joe, that is an interesting thought.

01:04:03.880 --> 01:04:08.260
But a little strategy, if you will, you have there with the best of 89.

01:04:09.180 --> 01:04:15.820
And where I sit right now on DuckTales is there is a case to be made for DuckTales Remastered,

01:04:15.820 --> 01:04:19.460
a game that we did not review on this podcast.

01:04:19.520 --> 01:04:25.480
And I didn't play it, so I don't even know if it's like actually like true and faithful and better.

01:04:26.120 --> 01:04:29.660
It could be a case that like, oh, well, it's been remastered and it's really fun there.

01:04:29.660 --> 01:04:33.720
And it's expanded upon and it has animated cut scenes and it includes the voice cast.

01:04:33.820 --> 01:04:37.500
So it's all the things that people probably wanted out of the NES DuckTales now better.

01:04:37.500 --> 01:04:39.980
Because they didn't change the levels or anything.

01:04:40.100 --> 01:04:43.400
They just took them and expanded them and added new ones, in fact.

01:04:44.580 --> 01:04:47.320
But like, you know, there's also something to say about like, you know,

01:04:47.340 --> 01:04:49.260
just because you make a game longer doesn't mean it's better.

01:04:49.360 --> 01:04:52.400
I mean, I'm starting to figure that out a lot about just video games in general.

01:04:52.580 --> 01:04:56.900
Is that these newer titles can't really hold my interest as well as these NES games.

01:04:56.900 --> 01:05:00.740
Not because I'm like being indoctrinated by playing this podcast.

01:05:01.000 --> 01:05:05.500
It's that I'm realizing some of these games are really tight, fun experiences in a short burst.

01:05:05.500 --> 01:05:11.640
That doesn't require, you know, hours upon hours of your time doing the same systems.

01:05:11.960 --> 01:05:16.960
And just, you know, slowly feeding you a drip feed of content as you go along the way.

01:05:17.140 --> 01:05:19.440
Who knows? Maybe that's what DuckTales Remastered is.

01:05:19.540 --> 01:05:23.680
So I can't say that DuckTales Remastered is going to inform my opinion here

01:05:23.680 --> 01:05:26.420
on whether DuckTales goes on the Essential Games list or not.

01:05:26.600 --> 01:05:30.720
What is going to inform my opinion here, though, is that Joe is on the fence

01:05:30.720 --> 01:05:35.480
about whether DuckTales should be on the Essential Games list.

01:05:35.620 --> 01:05:43.800
And where I feel like this is better solved is rather than me putting it on the Essential Games list right now

01:05:43.800 --> 01:05:49.500
and making it harder to remove, I'd rather see us go through the rest of 89.

01:05:49.500 --> 01:05:51.080
This guy's doing this meta game and shit.

01:05:51.300 --> 01:05:57.840
This is real. Play all these other games and then decide whether we can get to a unanimous vote on a game like DuckTales.

01:05:58.060 --> 01:06:00.120
Because I could see the argument for both.

01:06:00.260 --> 01:06:04.660
I think when Sean was talking, he had me, you know, thinking like, yeah, it is an Essential Game.

01:06:04.780 --> 01:06:08.560
And when Joe was talking, he reminded me, oh, well, you know, yeah, it is kind of a short experience

01:06:08.560 --> 01:06:14.180
that doesn't offer much variety other than, you know, the thematic changes of each level.

01:06:14.300 --> 01:06:18.300
Like, it's not expansive compared to the other games on the Essential Games list.

01:06:18.300 --> 01:06:23.300
However, a tight experience is a tight experience and it's probably worth experiencing today.

01:06:23.620 --> 01:06:27.380
So definitely, you know, both of you agree that this is a great NES game.

01:06:27.520 --> 01:06:30.220
It's just the problem of is it an Essential Game?

01:06:30.380 --> 01:06:37.200
And so I'd like to, you know, just pause on that for a second.

01:06:37.200 --> 01:06:44.000
And instead, I'm going to vote no so that we can revisit this topic probably, who knows what, a whole year from now?

01:06:44.120 --> 01:06:45.180
When is the best of 89?

01:06:45.180 --> 01:06:46.120
I don't know.

01:06:46.560 --> 01:06:47.860
The game is evolving.

01:06:48.100 --> 01:06:50.680
The game of this podcast is evolving now.

01:06:50.960 --> 01:06:51.800
And I like it.

01:06:52.460 --> 01:06:55.680
But I didn't do that for Air Fortress for more specific reasons.

01:06:55.880 --> 01:06:58.120
You know, I feel like it because I went last there, too.

01:06:58.220 --> 01:07:00.200
And I just felt like, no, that's not an Essential Game.

01:07:00.340 --> 01:07:01.280
With DuckTales, I don't know.

01:07:01.340 --> 01:07:02.340
I'm still kind of on the fence.

01:07:02.460 --> 01:07:06.220
But I'd rather us be unanimous on a game like DuckTales than unanimous on a game like Air Fortress.

01:07:06.220 --> 01:07:10.880
I feel like, you know, at this point, we have to take a bunch of games off the Essential Games list.

01:07:10.980 --> 01:07:15.080
Like if we're going, if this is the way we're going about it.

01:07:15.260 --> 01:07:18.060
Just because, you know, now I'm thinking like, you're right.

01:07:18.200 --> 01:07:26.180
There's a lot of games that I don't think fit that rubric that you're judging this one on.

01:07:27.200 --> 01:07:31.580
Well, here's something I wanted to say in response to what you said, Mike.

01:07:31.740 --> 01:07:32.920
Which is that I want to be clear.

01:07:33.440 --> 01:07:37.920
I am never of the opinion that longer equals better.

01:07:38.340 --> 01:07:41.840
And that's not what I meant as far as like there's not enough to this game.

01:07:42.020 --> 01:07:44.740
That there's literally like it's too short.

01:07:45.040 --> 01:07:47.880
Which like I think that it could help to make this longer.

01:07:48.080 --> 01:07:49.320
But I just think that you need to make.

01:07:49.440 --> 01:07:52.600
I think that the game could be a little deeper if that makes sense.

01:07:52.720 --> 01:07:54.680
Like there's all these like little things that are introduced.

01:07:54.680 --> 01:07:57.640
But I want to really get into these themes.

01:07:57.820 --> 01:08:00.480
And like use these new gameplay elements.

01:08:00.660 --> 01:08:02.140
And again, like I never played Shovel Knight.

01:08:02.420 --> 01:08:07.040
But from what I understand from that game is it takes all these little things that it introduces to you.

01:08:07.120 --> 01:08:10.660
And it builds them into like things you have to think about differently.

01:08:10.900 --> 01:08:11.760
And approach different ways.

01:08:12.140 --> 01:08:13.520
And DuckTales did that a little bit.

01:08:13.600 --> 01:08:17.440
But I wanted it to kind of, I wanted it to do a little more.

01:08:17.960 --> 01:08:19.740
Oh yeah, no, I completely understand that, Joe.

01:08:19.860 --> 01:08:23.000
I was just saying that like just because a game gets remastered.

01:08:23.000 --> 01:08:25.780
Doesn't mean that the remastered is default, the better.

01:08:26.160 --> 01:08:27.340
Right, right, right, right.

01:08:28.000 --> 01:08:36.400
But I also don't think that, I can't use a game that I haven't played.

01:08:36.580 --> 01:08:42.620
Like I will say that if a game falls into the same category of a game that we're reviewing.

01:08:42.620 --> 01:08:43.720
And I've played it.

01:08:44.060 --> 01:08:47.520
And I think it's close enough that it's like, well, just play that instead.

01:08:47.780 --> 01:08:49.800
But you're using a game you haven't played.

01:08:49.800 --> 01:08:51.020
I don't know.

01:08:51.460 --> 01:08:55.300
Well, Shovel Knight is not what is making me keep it off.

01:08:55.320 --> 01:08:59.240
I'm just using that as an example because it looks like it's similar.

01:08:59.780 --> 01:09:05.840
But taking other games, like any other game that has like a quote unquote gimmick to it.

01:09:05.980 --> 01:09:09.880
Like this gimmick being the pogo sticking thing or the different things it's adding.

01:09:10.060 --> 01:09:11.180
It's just like we talked about.

01:09:11.280 --> 01:09:16.120
It's adding things and it's not, they're not coming back ever.

01:09:16.280 --> 01:09:18.560
They happen one time and they don't go deeper.

01:09:18.560 --> 01:09:22.540
And I don't think I've done a great job of explaining what I mean by deeper.

01:09:22.780 --> 01:09:29.040
But particularly with platforms, I'm personally looking for like evolution of the gameplay.

01:09:29.280 --> 01:09:32.500
And Shovel Knight was a stupid example because obviously I haven't played it.

01:09:32.620 --> 01:09:37.920
But take like Super Mario Brothers or Crash Bandicoot, which both introduce really good

01:09:37.920 --> 01:09:40.060
gameplay and DuckTales does that too.

01:09:40.260 --> 01:09:45.700
But in Super Mario Brothers, that evolves more throughout the experience and gets more challenging

01:09:45.700 --> 01:09:49.140
and intricate, which is what keeps me wanting to move forward.

01:09:49.440 --> 01:09:55.220
So like, you know, even if you look at something like Mega Man, which doesn't necessarily evolve

01:09:55.220 --> 01:10:00.940
in challenge since you can play in any order, it like it makes up for it because you evolve

01:10:00.940 --> 01:10:05.760
throughout. And the levels introduce like new ways for you to approach them and new gameplay.

01:10:07.140 --> 01:10:13.220
But with this game, it just it never felt like it got deeper in that sense or like too much

01:10:13.220 --> 01:10:18.920
deeper in that sense where like each level, while it feels like aesthetically different

01:10:18.920 --> 01:10:24.820
and maybe introduces like one instance of something unique, it just didn't seem to capitalize it

01:10:24.820 --> 01:10:27.780
enough. And it left me wanting more out of it, you know?

01:10:27.780 --> 01:10:33.220
And like, I guess the best example of it is like by the time I got to the final level

01:10:33.220 --> 01:10:36.600
of DuckTales and it was the same level I had already played.

01:10:36.600 --> 01:10:40.560
And now I'm on the third time I'm playing this level without really any changes or upgrades

01:10:40.560 --> 01:10:42.020
or anything new to experience.

01:10:42.520 --> 01:10:45.880
I was sort of feeling like I was kind of getting over it at that point.

01:10:46.060 --> 01:10:50.820
And like, I'm not looking right now looking like I'm so excited to jump back in and actually

01:10:50.820 --> 01:10:53.580
beat this game because I kind of feel like I got the whole picture already.

01:10:53.580 --> 01:10:59.560
And like, I know that all sounds really negative, but but I really think, you know, because I

01:10:59.560 --> 01:11:01.000
really do think this was a great game.

01:11:01.640 --> 01:11:07.100
I just I've come to want a little more out of something that I would vote essential.

01:11:07.460 --> 01:11:11.900
Yeah, I think, you know, what you're describing, some people might say it's just a short and

01:11:11.900 --> 01:11:14.580
sweet game, you know, like they it doesn't have many flaws.

01:11:14.580 --> 01:11:16.560
So they just, you know, made it what it was.

01:11:16.700 --> 01:11:18.920
And then they didn't expand on that.

01:11:19.080 --> 01:11:23.500
I think a lot of the games you were referencing, though, like calling out Mega Man 2, we've been

01:11:23.500 --> 01:11:24.660
doing that a bunch in the episode.

01:11:25.400 --> 01:11:27.100
I think that is a fair comparison.

01:11:27.300 --> 01:11:31.160
I don't you say Mega Man doesn't necessarily like get more challenging because you can go

01:11:31.160 --> 01:11:35.960
in any order. I think, like we said in the episode, that's something that's very interesting that you can

01:11:35.960 --> 01:11:39.420
choose any path and it matters in this game.

01:11:39.580 --> 01:11:41.400
You can choose any path and it doesn't matter.

01:11:41.940 --> 01:11:42.760
Yeah, no, totally.

01:11:42.900 --> 01:11:47.640
And particularly for, you know, for a platformer, that's like maybe it's just me, but that's

01:11:47.640 --> 01:11:49.060
what I'm looking for out of a platform.

01:11:49.200 --> 01:11:52.780
It's like some sort of evolution, even if you are choosing your own your own path.

01:11:52.780 --> 01:11:55.160
Like like Mega Man solved that problem.

01:11:55.360 --> 01:11:59.100
And this I felt like and I'm saying problems that I'm really just trying to explain why

01:11:59.100 --> 01:12:00.640
I don't think it's up to essential.

01:12:00.820 --> 01:12:02.700
I still do think it's a really good game.

01:12:03.220 --> 01:12:05.720
Just, you know, I'll be honest.

01:12:06.220 --> 01:12:10.980
After I played it, I read a bunch of like what people say about it in reviews and stuff.

01:12:11.080 --> 01:12:15.780
And like my experience wasn't it wasn't as good as everyone else's seemed to be.

01:12:15.920 --> 01:12:17.820
So like maybe there's a disconnect there.

01:12:17.960 --> 01:12:21.140
But yeah, that's kind of my overall feeling on it.

01:12:21.700 --> 01:12:26.180
Very intense. And the essential games list remains to be very intense, hotly debated.

01:12:26.440 --> 01:12:29.940
And some people will tell you that it's already invalid because we don't have certain games

01:12:29.940 --> 01:12:35.080
on it. So why not just add DuckTales to the list of invalidity that is the essential games list?

01:12:35.660 --> 01:12:39.040
Well, you know, there's always a chance for every NES game to be on the essential games

01:12:39.040 --> 01:12:43.100
list. I don't want people to feel like, you know, we were joking about the black bass, but there

01:12:43.100 --> 01:12:44.540
was a chance before that episode, right?

01:12:44.600 --> 01:12:45.640
We don't come in with judgment.

01:12:45.640 --> 01:12:47.260
I don't come in with any judgment.

01:12:47.460 --> 01:12:51.720
So if I told you guys that they were going to make a whole video game based around Fester,

01:12:51.940 --> 01:12:56.400
Uncle Fester from the Addams family and call it Fester's Quest, and we'd be playing it next

01:12:56.400 --> 01:13:02.280
week. You guys wouldn't just say like, oh, Mike, that's based on a side character from a TV

01:13:02.280 --> 01:13:04.540
show that I didn't have any affiliation with.

01:13:04.700 --> 01:13:06.060
That's not going on the essential games list.

01:13:06.200 --> 01:13:07.820
You'd give that the honest fair shake.

01:13:07.820 --> 01:13:09.400
Well, now I'm not.

01:13:12.000 --> 01:13:13.160
What's wrong with Uncle Fester?

01:13:13.260 --> 01:13:14.160
Why can't he have his own game?

01:13:14.340 --> 01:13:15.140
And he does, by the way.

01:13:15.240 --> 01:13:16.400
It's called Fester's Quest.

01:13:17.080 --> 01:13:17.880
I think that.

01:13:17.920 --> 01:13:19.160
And it's what we'll be playing next week.

01:13:22.200 --> 01:13:26.080
And also, you know, for those of you who are looking for more Nostalgia content, keep

01:13:26.080 --> 01:13:31.980
in mind that we have a Patreon now for a little show called Nostalgia Bites, little bite-sized

01:13:31.980 --> 01:13:34.960
episodes where we play through the Famicom library.

01:13:34.960 --> 01:13:40.500
So maybe it should be called like Famstalgia Bites instead because it's Famicom instead

01:13:40.500 --> 01:13:42.080
of Ness. But whatever.

01:13:42.280 --> 01:13:46.380
You get the idea. We've done three episodes already, but technically four games.

01:13:46.500 --> 01:13:47.420
Try to figure that one out.

01:13:47.800 --> 01:13:50.300
Hint. We recorded two games in one episode.

01:13:50.500 --> 01:13:56.360
The next game that we're doing, Antarctic Adventure, it's like, you know, a penguin version

01:13:56.360 --> 01:13:58.640
of Slalom with some racing aspects.

01:13:59.120 --> 01:14:00.180
What's not to like?

01:14:00.340 --> 01:14:02.000
What's not to try?

01:14:02.000 --> 01:14:05.460
What's not to give us some money to hear?

01:14:27.760 --> 01:14:28.720
What's not to try?
